[31;1m468:   how_label:"Protocol", how_title:"How a week works",[0m
[31;1m469:   how_sub:"The protocol is the same every week and allows no exceptions. Everything that happens is archived with the system's real time. In a prospective run only what was available before the cutoff counts; the runs on this page are historical reconstructions with data captured after the cutoffs, and are declared as such.",[0m
[31;1m470:   steps:[[0m
[31;1m471:     {when:"Sunday 18:00",h:"Cutoff",p:"The information window closes. In a prospective run only what was published and archived before this time enters; in the reconstructions on this page the data were captured on 9–10 September 2026, after every cutoff, and the cutoff only filters by session date."},[0m
[31;1m472:     {when:"Monday 08:30",h:"Deadline",p:"Each forecaster delivers its five-stock list. It is archived with a real timestamp and a content signature."},[0m
[31;1m473:     {when:"Monday · open",h:"Simulated entry",p:"Buy at the opening price, with commission, slippage and the scenario's lot size."},[0m
[31;1m474:     {when:"Friday · close",h:"Simulated exit",p:"Sell at the last close of the week, with sales tax. If there is no session, the exit waits for the next one."},[0m
[31;1m475:     {when:"Afterwards",h:"Measurement",p:"Each portfolio is paired with the same week's random control and the excess is estimated with block bootstrap."}[0m
[31;1m476:   ],[0m
[31;1m477:   fc_title:"Three forecasters, one yardstick",[0m
[31;1m478:   fc_cards:{Q0:"A rule with no learning: buy the five stocks that rose the most over the last 20 sessions. The simplest possible yardstick.",Q1:"A tabular model (ridge + LightGBM) on weekly return ranks. Trained only on labels already known at the cutoff, retrained every four weeks.",A1:"Five random stocks from the same eligible universe, same seed every run. If a model does not beat chance, there is no signal to defend."},[0m
[31;1m479:   controls_title:"Controls that make the measurement trustworthy",[0m
[31;1m480:   controls:[[0m
[31;1m481:     {b:"Strict clock (point-in-time)",p:"Every datum carries three times: when it became available, when it was first seen and when it was archived. None is ever rewritten. In reconstructions the archive time is later than the cutoff and availability is marked as a conservative inference."},[0m
[31;1m482:     {b:"Append-only archive",p:"Captures, packets and lists are stored with a content hash in a manifest that only grows. A single altered byte is detected."},[0m
[31;1m483:     {b:"Verified readmission",p:"In prospective mode, when a packet is reloaded every document is re-derived from the original bytes and anything that does not match is rejected without exposing its content. In historical reconstructions documents are declared unverified unless the extractor registry is supplied; the extractor for multi-capture series is still pending."},[0m
[31;1m484:     {b:"Explicit costs and real lots",p:"Commission, sales tax, slippage and 1,000-share (or odd) lots are applied with exact arithmetic."},[0m
[31;1m485:     {b:"Paired random control",p:"The only valid comparison is against a random portfolio from the same week with the same exposure."},[0m
[31;1m486:     {b:"No real orders",p:"The lab never connects to a broker or handles credentials. It only simulates and archives."}[0m
